-----------------------------------------------------------------

1. HierText and Open Images material (CC BY-SA 4.0)

   The images, crops, quoted lines and word pairs taken from HierText, and the tables derived
   from it, in reports/, docs/RELEASE_NOTES_v1.0.md, docs/FINAL_VALIDATION.md, MODEL_CARD.md,
   release/huggingface/README.md and research/paper/ come from HierText (Long et al.,
   "Towards End-to-End Unified Scene Text Detection and Layout Analysis", CVPR 2022,
   https://github.com/google-research-datasets/hiertext). HierText is released under
   CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), and this material is shared
   under the same licence. Its images come from Open Images
   (https://storage.googleapis.com/openimages/web/index.html), which lists them as CC BY 2.0
   (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/) and gives no warranty about the licence of
   any one image. The material was changed: crops were cut from the images, resized and
   converted to grey scale, and previews show them after the augmentations named there. Author
   and source are not recorded per image; line keys begin with the HierText image ID.

   This notice is the attribution for that material in full. The list of report files written
   before they carried their own attribution line is in reports/README.md, "Attribution of
   HierText and Open Images material". reports/ is in the tagged GitHub repository but is left
   out of source archives made with git archive and of the Zenodo deposit (.gitattributes,
   export-ignore); DATASETS.md, which records the licences of every dataset, is in both.

2. Quoted GDC lines and GDC word pairs (their sources' licences)

   reports/error_cases/phase15/ quotes lines from the openly licensed and public-domain source
   documents of the project's GDC test set, each with its key, URL and licence, and
   reports/confusion_analysis/GW-REC-040/ holds GDC word-confusion pairs pooled over all of its
   source documents. These remain under the licences of their sources, which are listed in
   DATASETS.md, "GDC source documents". Like the rest of reports/, these files are in the tagged
   GitHub repository only (see item 1).

3. Data records under data/manifests/

   The manifests record identifiers, URLs, sizes and hashes of third-party datasets, weights and
   evaluators. They are data records about those sources, not code, and the sources themselves
   keep their own terms (DATASETS.md).

